{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/dean-of-the-school-of-business-langston-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Dean of the School of Business",
      "description": "Dean of the School of Business - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Dean of the School of Business - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Dean of the School of Business 495152 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Faculty PhD Campus LANGSTON Contact Name & Email Human Resources, luhumanresources@langston.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $125,000 - $130,000 Commensurate with education and experience Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume/curriculum vitae, cover letter, official transcript and three professional recommendation letters About this Position Langston University invites applications and nominations for the position of Dean of the School of Business. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the School and provides visionary, strategic, and collaborative leadership to advance excellence in teaching, scholarship, student success, workforce development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will join the University during a transformative period focused on enrollment growth, academic innovation, student persistence and completion, workforce alignment, and expanded research and partnership opportunities. The Dean will play a critical role in positioning the School of Business as a regional and national leader in business education, entrepreneurship, analytics, and applied learning while advancing the mission of Oklahoma’s only historically Black college and university. The Dean is expected to foster a culture of academic excellence, innovation, accountability, and collegiality while strengthening relationships with industry, alumni, government agencies, and philanthropic partners. Required Qualifications Ph.D./Ed.D. Business, Accounting, Finance, Management or closely related discipline from an accredited institution. (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) 10 years of progressive administrative experience. Qualifications appropriate for appointment as an associate professor or professor. Significant academic leadership experience at the department chair, associate dean, dean, or equivalent level. Demonstrated success in strategic planning, budgeting, personnel management, and academic administration. Evidence of scholarly achievement and commitment to academic excellence. Strong communication, interpersonal, and consensus-building skills. Demonstrated commitment to student success. Preferred Qualifications Experience with AACSB accreditation or other specialized accreditation processes. Experience at an HBCU, land-grant institution, or mission-driven public university. Demonstrated success in fundraising, grant development, and external partnership cultivation. Experience developing online, hybrid, executive, or workforce-focused academic programs. Industry or entrepreneurial experience that enhances business-school leadership. Knowledge of emerging trends in business education, analytics, AI applications, entrepreneurship, and workforce development. Langston University is an equal opportunity employer. Our hiring decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and institutional needs, ensuring equal opportunities for all individuals, regardless of race, gender, age, disability, or other protected characteristics. We welcome qualified applicants who share our commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, and fostering a vibrant campus culture. For more information, please contact luhumanresources@langston.edu. You may also be interested in Assistant Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Food Innovation - 2187 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Assistant Professor, Reference & Instruction Librarian-1789 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Professional Practice in Entrepreneurship 221243 Payne County. Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 22b2fbe4 Last Name (required) 3797567c Email (required) a4f0be33 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
