    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/dean-of-the-school-of-nursing-and-health-professions-2050-langston-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions -2050",
      "description": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions -2050 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions -2050 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions -2050 495146 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Faculty PhD Campus LANGSTON Contact Name & Email Nika Wilson, luhumanresources@langston.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $125,000 - $130,000 Commensurate with education and experience Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter, official transcript and three professional recommendation letters. About this Position Langston University invites applications and nominations for the position of Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean serves as the chief academic and administrative officer for the School and provides visionary leadership for nursing and allied health education, workforce development, clinical partnerships, student success, accreditation, and community engagement. The Dean will lead a dynamic and growing academic unit dedicated to preparing highly skilled, compassionate, and culturally responsive healthcare professionals. The successful candidate will advance innovative academic programming, strengthen healthcare partnerships, support student achievement, and position the School as a leader in addressing healthcare workforce shortages across Oklahoma and beyond. This is an exceptional opportunity for a collaborative leader committed to excellence in nursing and health professions education, clinical partnerships, faculty development, research, and public service. Required Qualifications: Ph.D./Ed.D. Earned doctorate in nursing, nursing education, healthcare administration, public health, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Master’s degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Experience: 10 years of progressive administrative experience. Experience with ACEN, or other nursing accreditation processes. Experience leading nursing or allied health programs at an HBCU or public university. Demonstrated success in clinical partnership development and healthcare workforce initiatives. Experience with grant-funded initiatives, simulation laboratories, online learning, and interprofessional education. Evidence of successful fundraising and external engagement. Understanding of healthcare workforce trends and rural/community health needs. Record of successful teaching, scholarship, and service. Demonstrated knowledge of accreditation, assessment, regulatory compliance, and program administration. 10 years of progressive administrative experience. Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: Current or eligible RN licensure in Oklahoma. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications Current or eligible RN licensure in Oklahoma. Langston University is an equal opportunity employer. Our hiring decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and institutional needs, ensuring equal opportunities for all individuals, regardless of race, gender, age, disability, or other protected characteristics. We welcome qualified applicants who share our commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, and fostering a vibrant campus culture. For more information, please contact luhumanresources@langston.edu. You may also be interested in Nursing Instructor/Assistant Professor (Langston Campus)-1111 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Adjunct Instructor-Healthcare Administration Program-2135 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Assistant Professor/Site Director School of Nursing (Langston Campus) - 1064 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Apply Now! First