    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-nutritional-sciences-and-food-innovation-2187-langston-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Food Innovation - 2187",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Food Innovation - 2187 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Food Innovation - 2187 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Food Innovation - 2187 494749 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Faculty PhD Campus LANGSTON Contact Name & Email Kenyette Saywon, kenyette.saywon@langston.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $74,000 - $77,000 Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter, official transcript and three professional recommendation letters. POSITION SUMMARY: The Langston University Sherman Lewis School of Agriculture and Applied Sciences seeks an Assistant Professor of Food Innovation and Nutritional Sciences. The successful candidate will advance the School’s land-grant mission by developing a high-impact research program, participate in product innovation activities starting with locally produced items, engage with stakeholders through Extension, deliver excellence in teaching, and engage in scholarly service. This position has an expected Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) involving all three aspects of the Land-Grant mission—for example: 50% research, 30% extension, 20% teaching (must equal 100%). The final FTE will, however, will be aligned with the strengths of the individual selected for the position among other factors. Key Responsibilities: · Research: Develop and sustain a nationally recognized, research program focusing on the food innovations, intersection of human nutrition, and health, for e.g., functional foods, molecular nutrition, microbiome-food interactions. · Teaching: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as food microbiology, nutritional biochemistry, Food Chemistry, or Sustainable Food Systems. Mentor graduate students (MS) and advise undergraduate students. · Extension and Service: Conduct a wide array of engagements with stakeholders in Oklahoma and beyond. Participate in schoolwide, university committees, and contribute to professional societies. Engage in outreach activities that support the local and scientific community. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Food Science, Human Nutrition, Nutritional Biology, or a closely related field.(degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Evidence of a strong scholarly record. Demonstrated potential to secure external funding (grants/contracts) to support research initiatives. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Excellent communication skills and demonstrated ability to teach at the university level. Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral or other professional research experience. Postdoctoral or other professional research experience. Experience in interdisciplinary collaborations. Experience with on-site and online pedagogy. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies Ability to write successful grant proposals. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to operate a personal computer and related software applications. Team oriented and ability to foster a cooperative and customer-friendly work environment. Knowledge of faculty and/or staff hiring procedures. Langston University is an equal opportunity employer. Our hiring decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and institutional needs, ensuring equal opportunities for all individuals, regardless of race, gender, age, disability, or other protected characteristics. We welcome qualified applicants who share our commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, and fostering a vibrant campus culture. For more information, please contact luhumanresources@langston.edu. You may also be interested in Assistant Professor of Animal Science-2185 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Animal Science Research Scientist and Extension Specialist -2149* Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Director of Career and Professional Development -1366 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Apply Now! First Name (required) f073b801 Last Name (required) 0d4e9614 Email (required) 6d607d1d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or ale