    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/school-of-arts-sciences-chemistry-physical-science-department-adjunct-instructor-1841-langston-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "School of Arts & Sciences/Chemistry & Physical Science Department Adjunct Instructor-1841",
      "description": "School of Arts & Sciences/Chemistry & Physical Science Department Adjunct Instructor-1841 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States School of Arts & Sciences/Chemistry & Physical Science Department Adjunct Instructor-1841 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode School of Arts & Sciences/Chemistry & Physical Science Department Adjunct Instructor-1841 493704 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Adjunct/Temp Faculty Master's degree Campus LANGSTON Contact Name & Email Nika Wilson, luhumanresources@langston.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length 6 months or less Hiring Range Determined by class size and number of courses Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter, transcript(s) and three professional recommendation letters. About this Position The Department of Chemistry and Physical Sciences is seeking a qualified Adjunct Instructor to teach lower-division courses, including Introductory Chemistry, General Chemistry I & II laboratory/lecture support (as needed), Physics, and Physical Science for non-majors. Candidates with a Master’s degree will be considered for lower-division teaching assignments. Applicants holding a Ph.D. in Chemistry or a closely related discipline may also be eligible to teach upper-division coursework based on departmental needs. Why Join Langston University? Be part of a vibrant academic community committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service Inspire and mentor students in a student-centered learning environment Flexible teaching load ideal for working professionals Opportunity to contribute to the continued success of Oklahoma’s only Historically Black College/University (HBCU) Responsibilities Teach assigned undergraduate courses in Chemistry and/or Physical Science. Prepare and deliver course materials, including lectures, assignments, assessments, and laboratory activities (where applicable). Maintain consistent communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments and exams. Hold office hours (virtual or in-person) for student support. Follow departmental and university guidelines regarding instruction, assessment, and academic policies. Collaborate with full-time faculty as needed to ensure instructional consistency across sections. Required Qualifications Master's Master's degree in chemistry, Chemistry Education, Physics, Physical Science, or a closely related field. (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Demonstrated ability to effectively teach at the undergraduate level. Demonstrated passion for teaching and student success Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong oral and written communication skills Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Commitment to fostering an inclusive, supportive learning environment Preferred Qualification Ph.D. in Chemistry or a closely related discipline (required for teaching upper-division coursework). Prior college-level teaching experience. Experience teaching non-majors and/or introductory STEM courses. Familiarity with learning management systems (e.g., Blackboard, Canvas). Demonstrated experience in facilitating the success of students from diverse backgrounds. Langston University is an equal opportunity employer. Our hiring decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and institutional needs, ensuring equal opportunities for all individuals, regardless of race, gender, age, disability, or other protected characteristics. We welcome qualified applicants who share our commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, and fostering a vibrant campus culture. For more information, please contact luhumanresources@langston.edu. You may also be