    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/school-of-education-and-behavioral-sciences-adjunct-instructors-1843-langston-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "School of Education and Behavioral Sciences Adjunct Instructors-1843",
      "description": "School of Education and Behavioral Sciences Adjunct Instructors-1843 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States School of Education and Behavioral Sciences Adjunct Instructors-1843 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode School of Education and Behavioral Sciences Adjunct Instructors-1843 493677 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Adjunct/Temp Faculty Master's degree Campus LANGSTON Contact Name & Email nika wilson, luhumanresources@langston.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length 6 months or less Hiring Range Per-course compensation is commensurate with education and experience and based on enrollment. Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter, official transcript(s) and three professional recommendation letters. About this Position The Langston University School of Education and Behavioral Sciences is building a pool of qualified adjunct instructors and invites applications to join our team. We are seeking adjunct faculty in the following departments Psychology Education Health, Physical Education and Recreation Rehabilitation Services Library Science. We welcome dynamic educators who are committed to delivering engaging, high-quality learning experiences for students pursuing a Bachelor of Science degree. This role provides an exciting opportunity to inspire the next generation of scholars while contributing to the University’s mission of academic excellence, scholarship, and service. Required Qualifications Master's degree in the relevant discipline (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Prior teaching experience at the college or university level preferred. Professional experience in one or more of the following disciplines: Psychology Education Health, Physical Education, and Recreation Rehabilitation Services Library Science Required Experience Experience mentoring, advising, or supporting students in their academic and professional development. Demonstrated ability to design and deliver engaging instruction in both traditional classroom and online learning environments. Evidence of scholarly engagement, professional practice, or community service aligned with the mission of Langston University. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D./Ed.D. Langston University is an equal opportunity employer. Our hiring decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and institutional needs, ensuring equal opportunities for all individuals, regardless of race, gender, age, disability, or other protected characteristics. We welcome qualified applicants who share our commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, and fostering a vibrant campus culture. For more information, please contact luhumanresources@langston.edu. You may also be interested in School of Arts & Sciences/Social Sciences Department Adjunct Instructor-1841 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Academic Advisor & Success Coach-1104 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Outreach and Engagement Specialist, 001369 Langston VP OPERATIONS (LU) Apply Now! First Name (required) de66731c Last Name (required) a3875916 Email (required) 9ae0243c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
