    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-school-of-nursing-health-professions-1844-langston-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing & Health Professions -1844",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing & Health Professions -1844 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing & Health Professions -1844 - Langston, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing & Health Professions -1844 495390 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Adjunct/Temp Faculty Master's degree Campus LANGSTON Contact Name & Email Human Resources, luhumanresources@langston.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length 12 months or less Hiring Range $ - $ Commensurate with education and experience Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume/curriculum vitae, cover letter, official transcript and three professional recommendation letters. About this Position Langston University School of Nursing invites applications for part-time adjunct nursing faculty to support the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program. Adjunct faculty may be assigned didactic, clinical, laboratory, simulation, or other instructional responsibilities based on academic preparation, clinical expertise, program needs, and course availability. The successful candidate will contribute to student learning and professional development while supporting the mission, policies, curriculum, and academic standards of Langston University and the School of Nursing and Health Professions. TEACHING AREAS Adjunct faculty may be assigned to teach in one or more of the following areas based on expertise and departmental needs: Childrearing (Pediatrics) Childbearing (Obstetrics) Adult Health (Medical-Surgical) Psychosocial/Mental Health Nursing Assignments may include didactic, clinical, laboratory, and/or simulation instruction. Clinical assignments may include weekday, evening, and weekend shifts depending on course and clinical-site needs. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Deliver high-quality didactic, clinical, laboratory, and/or simulation instruction consistent with approved course objectives, syllabi, curriculum requirements, and professional nursing standards. Provide safe and effective clinical supervision and maintain appropriate oversight of students in assigned clinical settings. Evaluate student learning and performance using approved assessment methods, grading criteria, clinical evaluation tools, and rubrics. Maintain accurate and timely records of attendance, grades, student progress, clinical performance, and other required course documentation. Provide timely feedback to students and communicate academic or clinical concerns to the course faculty, Site Director, and/or Dean as appropriate. Utilize evidence-based practice, current clinical standards, and culturally responsive teaching strategies in the learning environment. Follow established course materials, learning activities, policies, and procedures; coordinate with lead/course faculty to promote consistency across course sections and clinical groups. Participate in orientation, required faculty meetings, course coordination meetings, training, and accreditation-related activities as requested and applicable to the adjunct assignment. Assist with student remediation and academic support related to the assigned course or clinical experience, as appropriate. Maintain current clinical competence and required professional credentials for assigned teaching responsibilities. Serve as a professional role model and maintain professional communication and conduct with students, faculty, staff, clinical partners, and community members. Adhere to all Langston University, School of Nursing and Health Professions, clinical agency, state, and professional policies, procedures, and standards. Complete required university and clinical-agency onboarding, compliance, and documentation within established timelines. Other duties related to the adjunct teaching assignment as assigned by the Dean and/or Site Director. ADJUNCT APPOINTMENT EXPECTATIONS Adjunct appointments are made on a course-by-course or semester basis according to program needs and do not guarantee continued employment or future teaching assignments. Teaching schedules and workload are determined by course enrollment, clinical-site availability, faculty expertise, and program needs. Adjunct faculty are expected to be available for scheduled instruction, student evaluation, course-related communication, and required meetings associated with the assigned course or clinical experience. All required licenses, certifications, health/compliance documentation, and clinical-agency requirements must remain current throughout the appointment. Required Qualifications Master's Master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Unencumbered RN license in Oklahoma or eligibility for Oklahoma licensure; required licensure must be obtained before the teaching assignment begins. (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Minimum two (2) years of recent clinical experience as a Registered Nurse. Clinical expertise appropriate to the assigned course or clinical area. Ability to teach and evaluate students effectively in clinical, laboratory, simulation, and/or classroom settings. Ability to use instructional technology and learning-management systems required for assigned courses. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong oral, written, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. Ability to teach and evaluate students effectively in clinical, laboratory, simulation, and/or classroom settings. Available to meet with students as needed Commitment to inclusive excellence and the mission of Langston University. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D./Ed.D. Doctorate in Nursing (PhD, EdD, DNP) or a related discipline. Prior teaching experience in a BSN or higher nursing education program. Experience with Canvas. Experience with curriculum implementation, accreditation processes, student assessment, and program evaluation. Working Conditions standard office & classroom environment clinical & laboratory setting Langston University is an equal opportunity employer. Our hiring decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and institutional needs, ensuring equal opportunities for all individuals, regardless of race, gender, age, disability, or other protected characteristics. We welcome qualified applicants who share our commitment to academic excellence, community engagement, and fostering a vibrant campus culture. For more information, please contact luhumanresources@langston.edu. You may also be interested in There are currently no jobs matching this criteria. Apply Now! First Name (required) b8b4f1db Last Name (required) 4266f768 Email (required) 5db94d1f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
